# WP-207 §D: under --gc-sections an unchanged file's section dies (its only
# caller in a changed file stops calling it), revives, dies again.
proves: the revival of hop 2 left u.o's SECTIONS, HOLES and .symtab rows true, so the second death is a clean hole
source: WP-207 §D, the two- and three-hop series
edit: c.cc
link: main.o c.o u.o
cflags: -ffunction-sections
options: --gc-sections
expect-full: update-not-implemented (layout): every hop flips a section's liveness, which changes the stored placement (SECTIONS.bits, META.live_hash); `live` is judged against the front's mark and the image takes a new placement only from M2b-3 on (WP-225 gc-lift), so no hop expects a gc UPDATE: a hop that updates fails, a hop that falls back earlier (no-state, small-output) is n/a
compilers: gcc kiln
also-reversed: the first link never places u_helper (WP-207 §D: "also with the first link never placing it")
